    "<p>10 câu</p>\n<div>\n<div>\n<span>III</span>\n<div>\n<h2>PART III: READING COMPREHENSION (2.6 points)</h2>\n<p>Đọc hiểu đoạn văn &amp; điền từ thích hợp</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<span>10 câu • 2.6đ</span>\n</div>\n<!-- Task I: Cloze text (5 questions x 0.2 = 1.0p) -->\n<div>\n<div>\n<h3>\n<span>I. Circle the letter before the best answer to complete the passage. (1.0 pt)</span>\n\n</h3>\n</div>\n<!-- Cloze Passage Box -->\n<div>\n<h4>THREE WAYS TO BECOME HEALTHIER</h4>\n<p>\n              First of all, you need to eat the right kind of food. <strong>(1)_______</strong> is unhealthy, so you shouldn't eat it much. You shouldn't eat too much fatty food, too. Things like chips and burgers have a lot of fat. You should also try to <strong>(2) _______</strong> more fresh food and vegetables.\n            </p>\n<p>\n              Secondly, you <strong>(3) _______</strong> eat three meals a day so that you don't get hungry. You definitely shouldn't miss breakfast. When people don't eat breakfast, they often eat unhealthy snacks like chips during the day.\n            </p>\n<p>\n              Lastly, you don't need to be good at sports, <strong>(4) _____</strong> you should do some exercise. Exercise can be walking instead of taking the bus or using the stairs instead of the lift. You should do <strong>(5)_______</strong> morning exercise. Only about twenty minutes for each and three times a week is fine.\n            </p>\n</div>\n<!-- Cloze Options -->\n<div>\n<!-- R1 -->\n\n<!-- R2 -->\n\n<!-- R3 -->\n\n<!-- R4 -->\n\n<!-- R5 -->\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<!-- Task II: Reading Comprehension (Phong's school volunteer activities) -->\n<div>\n<div>\n<h3>\n<span>II. Read the passage and do the tasks as directed. (1.6 pt)</span>\n\n</h3>\n</div>\n<!-- Reading Text -->\n<div>\n<p>\n              Phong's school has a number of volunteer activities every summer. These activities include donating books to village children, tutoring kids in the neighbourhood, teaching English to primary students, reading books or cooking food for the needy. His school started the programme five years ago. Every student can join one or two activities.\n            </p>\n<p>\n              In the beginning, they thought about why they should join in the activities. They then thought about what activities they wanted to do. Those who like reading could choose to collect and donate books. Those who are good at English could tutor primary students. Finally, they signed up for the activities they chose. Their teachers often encourage them to stay committed. They also help when the students need it. Phong and his friends have a lot of fun and learn many things from doing these volunteer activities.\n            </p>\n</div>\n<!-- Section A: Answer the questions (3 questions x 0.4p = 1.2p) -->\n<div>\n<h4>A. Answer the questions (1.2 pt - Mỗi câu 0.4đ)</h4>\n<!-- QA 1 -->\n\n<!-- QA 2 -->\n\n<!-- QA 3 -->\n\n</div>\n<!-- Section B: Choose the best option (2 questions x 0.2p = 0.4p) -->\n<div>\n<h4>B. Choose the best option A, B, C or D to answer the questions (0.4 pt)</h4>\n<div>\n<!-- QB 4 -->\n\n<!-- QB 5 -->\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
